+MUTATION
+
+For the satisfying input n=1, change the required post-state from "0 1"
+(sequenceCodes(1)) to the false value "0" (sequenceCodes(0)).
+
+COMMAND
+kprove spec-vacuity.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY --dry-run
+
+EXIT STATUS
+0
+
+RELEVANT OUTPUT
+kore-exec .../audit-verification-kompiled/definition.kore --module VERIFICATION
+  --prove .../spec.kore --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY --output .../result.kore
+
+COMMAND
+kprove spec-vacuity.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY
+
+EXIT STATUS
+1
+
+RELEVANT OUTPUT
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+  The configuration's term doesn't unify with the destination's term and the
+  configuration cannot be rewritten further.
+  <k>
+    str ( iCons ( 48 , iCons ( 32 , iCons ( 49 , .IntSeq ) ) ) ) ~> .K
+  </k>
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further.
+
+The residual code sequence 48,32,49 is the actual "0 1", so the failure is the
+expected unmet result obligation, not a parse/build/backend failure.
